# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# M0 PoC probe worktree (never committed)
.temp/

# Cargo workspace build output. `/target/` is root-anchored and covers only the
# workspace member; a nested probe crate (e.g. the hand-io Rust peers under
# docs/probes/, which opt out with an empty `[workspace]`) builds to its own
# target dir and needs the second pattern. That pattern is depth-agnostic so a
# new nested crate cannot silently start committing a build tree.
/target/
docs/probes/**/target/

# Probe MEASUREMENT output — regenerable, so not committed.
#
# Three kinds, deliberately treated differently:
#   - `*-report.txt` IS committed (docs/probes/transport-lab/results/): every
#     claim in FINDINGS.md points at a figure in one, so they are the evidence.
#   - `*.json` is NOT: the probe writes it itself, and `matrix.json` alone was
#     1,273 lines for figures the report already states. Keeping it invited a
#     committed measurement to look authoritative after the machine changed.
#   - `Cargo.lock` in a probe crate is NOT: these are one-shot instruments, not
#     shipped artifacts, so pinning their dependency graph buys nothing. The
#     versions that matter are recorded in the relevant FINDINGS.md.
docs/probes/**/results/*.json
docs/probes/**/Cargo.lock

# Host sidecar artifact (built by scripts/build-host.ts into Tauri's
# externalBin input dir). The directory itself is tracked via
# src-tauri/binaries/README.md; only the generated binaries are ignored.
# (`host/dist/` needs no rule: the `dist` pattern above already covers it.)
/src-tauri/binaries/host-*
/src-tauri/binaries/.host-*.tmp-*
host/dist/

# bun cross-target compile cache (e.g. `bun build --compile --target
# bun-linux-*`); large and never committed.
host/.bun-cache/

# TypeScript incremental build info. Written by `tsc` whenever a config enables
# `incremental` / `composite`, and it records absolute-ish paths plus a graph that
# is meaningless on another machine. Found the hard way: running a throwaway
# `tsc -p <temp config>` at the repo root left `tsconfig.node.tsbuildinfo` behind
# as an untracked file that `git add -A` would have swept into a commit.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
